--- Linear algebra is rows of the builtin table (docs/bug-classes.md §4):
--- a matrix of the wrong shape, or one that is not positive definite, is
--- the reason one runtime function gives both modes. cholesky of such a
--- matrix panicked both, and a vector or a rectangle given to det or inv
--- panicked a kernel.
use math
a = [[4.0, 2.0], [2.0, 3.0]]
log[det[a]]
log[rank[a]]
log[len[svd[a]]]
log[norm[[3.0, 4.0]]]
log[norm[[3.0, 4.0], 1]]
log[dot[[1.0, 2.0], [3.0, 4.0]]]
log[triu[a]]
log[len[cholesky[a]]]
log[cholesky[[[1.0, 2.0], [2.0, 1.0]]]]
log['not reached']
